## CC BY 4.0 — the written work

Applies to:

- `Trauma Informed AI Safety Benchmark and Assurance Framework v1.1.pdf` and the `.docx` source
- `Trauma Informed AI Safety Benchmark and Assurance Framework v1.0.docx` (superseded, retained for citation continuity)
- `benchmark/items/` — the 187 public English seed items, their gold labels, trigger definitions and `SCHEMA.md`
- `benchmark/fixtures/`
- Every `README.md`, `TESTING.md`, and other prose in this repository

You may share and adapt this material, including commercially, for any purpose, provided you give
appropriate credit, link to the licence, and indicate whether you made changes. There are no
additional restrictions: adaptation of jurisdiction anchors, risk instruments and seed classes,
authoring of further benchmark items, and use in paid conformance assessment are all permitted.

**Attribution.** Use the citation in the README, and state clearly whether what you are distributing
is the framework as published or an adaptation of it. An adaptation must not be presented as the
Centre's published framework or as carrying the Centre's endorsement.

## Apache 2.0 — the software

Applies to:

- `benchmark/harness/` — the run, validate, judge, analyse and scoreboard tooling
- `benchmark/gui/` — the local control panel
- `benchmark/bridge/` — the product adapter
- Any other source file in this repository, including configuration templates

Apache 2.0 grants patent rights and requires that you keep the licence and copyright notices and
state significant changes. See [NOTICE](NOTICE).

## Not covered by either licence

- **`TIAB Journal Article Draft v0.7.docx`** — an unpublished manuscript in preparation for
  peer review. All rights reserved; it is present for co-author working purposes and is not
  released under CC BY or any other licence.
- **`benchmark/results/`** — run outputs. These are not part of the release, may contain material
  from systems belonging to third parties, and are excluded from version control by default.
- **Trade marks and names.** "The Digital Safeguard Centre" and the names of the authors are not
  licensed by either licence. Neither licence grants permission to imply endorsement, certification
  or conformance.
- **The Centre's own private assurance suite and casework-derived material**, which are not in this
  repository.

## Conformance and endorsement

Neither licence certifies anything. Conformance under the framework is self-assessed at L1
(declared) or L2 (verified), against evidence the adopter retains and discloses on request. No
party, including the Centre, certifies conformance, and no licence granted here should be read as
doing so.

## Warranty

Both licences disclaim warranties and liability, and those disclaimers are meant literally here.
This material concerns systems used by people at risk of serious harm. It is offered as a measure,
not as an assurance, and the adopter remains responsible for the safety of what they deploy.
